Transita Backend — Alembic Migrations
=====================================

Database migration tool for the Transita backend.

Quick Start
-----------
    # Apply all migrations to the database
    alembic upgrade head

    # Create a new migration (autogenerate from SQLAlchemy models)
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description"

    # Create an empty migration (manual)
    alembic revision -m "description"

    # View migration history
    alembic history

    # Check current migration version
    alembic current

    # Downgrade one step
    alembic downgrade -1

    # Downgrade to a specific revision
    alembic downgrade <revision_id>

Environment
-----------
DATABASE_URL is read from the environment. If not set, it falls back to
individual env vars: DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD, DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_NAME.

Example:
    DATABASE_URL=postgresql://admin:changeme@localhost:5432/san_antonio_db

Adding SQLAlchemy Models
------------------------
1. Create your model in app/models/ (e.g., app/models/base.py)
2. Import Base from your model in alembic/env.py:
       from app.models.base import Base
       target_metadata = Base.metadata
3. Run: alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add table name"
4. Review the generated migration in alembic/versions/
5. Apply: alembic upgrade head
